<title>GERMANY: Lan Chile adds fifth weekly Germany flight via Brazil.</title>
<headline>Lan Chile adds fifth weekly Germany flight via Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean carrier Lan Chile said it will add a fifth weekly flight to Germany from April 8.</p>
<p>Cargo manager Europe, Martin Rehs, said the Boeing 767-300 flights will be routed from Santiago via Sao Paulo and Madrid to Frankfurt.</p>
<p>&quot;We now have traffic rights for Brazil and there is a potential for small shipments,&quot; he told Reuters in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Lan Chile aimed to upgrade to daily flights to Germany later this year which would allow it to sell Brazil as a destination more actively, he added.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
</text>
